# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.backup.*

# ── Secrets & local credentials ───────────────────────────
# Never commit key material. Keys/ holds local credential docs.
Keys/
.env
.env.*
.northflank/
# Exception: client-side build env containing ONLY the public Sentry DSN
# (loaded by Vite at build time); safe to track, contains no secrets.
!frontend/.env.production

# ── Node / frontend build output ──────────────────────────
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/storybook-static/
coverage/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Runtime logs & traces ─────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ── Fidelity harness output (regenerated on every run) ────
# node frontend/scripts/fidelity-check.mjs --out <base> writes <base>.txt/.json
frontend/scripts/fidelity-report.*

# ── Agent session tooling ─────────────────────────────────
.zcode/
.continue/
.vscode/
.clinerules/

# ── Local-only files (owner-removed from GitHub) ───────────
RESTART-LOCAL.sh
architectural_philosophy
spec-techincal direction doc.pdf

#
# ── THE SESSION'S OWN WORKING FILES (2026-09-29) ─────────────────────────────
# By the owner's instruction, the same instruction that named n8n/ and the plans folder:
# "ignore: CANVAS-AND-CLEANUP, html_figma_visualization.html, prompt-input-section.html,
# START-HERE-INGESTION.md, RESTART-LOCAL.sh".
#
# All five are instruments the work was done WITH rather than the product itself: the notes
# written while the ingestion pipeline was built and measured, two standalone probe pages that
# exist to be opened and looked at, the canvas session record, and the local launcher above.
#
# RESTART-LOCAL.sh is listed twice on purpose. Its rule was added when it was first removed
# from the repository (01d4c51, "gitignore local-only files (owner-removed)"), and an ignore
# rule does nothing to a file git already tracks — it was re-added in 10af949 and has been
# tracked ever since. It is UNTRACKED in this change, which is what the rule always meant.
/CANVAS-AND-CLEANUP/
/START-HERE-INGESTION.md
/html_figma_visualization.html
/prompt-input-section.html

# ── Static assets & binary files ───────────────────────────────────
# Canvas lab workspace with large data files
canvas-lab/

# Pages export files (*.pages)
*.pages

# Local frontend gate-drive temporary file
frontend/gate-drive.mjs

# ── Reference repos (old snapshots — never tracked) ─────
dsmanager/

# ── Figma import cache (regenerated on every import) ────
frontend/.figma-cache/

# ── Catalog health reports (rewritten on every check) ─────
# frontend/catalog-audit/<pipeline>.json is the CHECKER'S OUTPUT, regenerated by
# RESTART-LOCAL.sh §4b on every boot and by `npm run build`. It is not source.
# The journal beside it at the repo root — catalog-audit/AI-notes.md — is NOT
# output, and it IS tracked: it is the only surviving copy of that document.
frontend/catalog-audit/
catalog-audit/*.json

# ── Agent-facing Figma notes (audience is an AI reader, not the repo) ──
# Kept on disk for local AI sessions. Not pushed to GitHub.
FIGMA/AGENT_BRIEF.md
FIGMA/AGENT_NODE_MAP.md
FIGMA/AGENT_OPEN_GAPS.md

# ── Ignored before commit (local working docs & agent instructions) ──
AGENT_NORTH_STAR.md
A2UI-Rules.md
WHAT-THEY-BUILT-WHAT-WE-BUILT.md
INDEX.md
ignore-for-commit/
AGENTS-instructions/
# The standing rules the agent loads at the start of every session — local, like the rest
# of the agent instructions above. See the file's own header for what it is.
AGENTS.md
#
# LOCAL-ONLY, BY THE OWNER'S DECISION (2026-09-17). The working registers and the
# catalog audit are the operator's own record of what is open and what the checker
# said — they are not published. TO-DO.md, open-items.json and corrections.json live in
# the working copy and in no clone, and so does the audit under catalog-audit/.
#
# This reverses an earlier rule that required the register to be tracked, on the
# grounds that a register git cannot see is one whose numbers drift unnoticed. That
# guard is intact where it matters: `check:open-items-register` still compares the
# numbers the register records against the numbers each run derives, and fails the
# build when they disagree. What is no longer asserted is visibility to git.
models/
retired-files/
TO-DO.md
open-items.json
corrections.json
catalog-audit/
frontend/catalog-audit/
# ── THE GOVERNANCE FOLDER (2026-09-18) ────────────────────────────────────────
# The plans and the history of the work, kept for the next inspection — same rule as the
# ledgers above: the operator's own record, local to this machine, in no clone.
governance/
#
# THE AGENTIC EDITOR'S OWN FOLDER, local-only by the owner's instruction (2026-09-18):
# "that folder is yours, I don't care what you do to it. It'll never be on GitHub."
# Its README, its CHANGELOG and its numbered chapters are the working record of the
# canvas work — a record for the session that writes it, not a document of the product.
AGENTIC_EDITOR/

#
# ── THE WORKING PLANS AND THE DESIGN CAPTURES (2026-09-29) ────────────────────
# The same rule as the governance folder above, and by the owner's instruction:
# "ignore: PLANS.AGENT, design". Both are the operator's own working record — the plans
# for the ingestion work, and the design captures read while it was built (VALUES.json,
# chat-column.json, node-census.json …). They are read and written locally and belong to
# no clone. The copies under frontend/src/design/ that were tracked are removed in the
# same change, so nothing of either survives in the history.
/PLANS.AGENT/
/design/

#
# THE DESIGNER PROFILE — local-only by the owner instruction (2026-09-19):
# "put it in the gitignore, I sure as hell don't want anybody to see it."
DESIGNER-PROFILE.md

#
# ── THE ROOT'S LOOSE DOWNLOADS (2026-09-19) ───────────────────────────────────
# Design references and stock art that sit at the repository root and are NOT source: the
# app's artwork lives in frontend/src/assets, and that is where anything used gets copied.
# Two of these were un-ignored and `git add -A` would sweep them in — 55 MB of extracted
# wave art and a 39 MB zip among them (measured 2026-09-19). The owner, on the repository's
# weight: "Ignore, I don't want that 5 MB 500 MB whatever it is, don't put that."
# Root-level only (the leading slash), so nothing under frontend/ or backend/ is affected.
/data-wave-background/
/data-wave-background.zip
/*.zip
/*.jpg
/*.png
/images/

# ── THE VENDORED REFERENCE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The TrueForge codebase, copied into this repository as a reference to READ — its agent
# loop, its skill handling, its connection client — while the Phase 3 work was designed
# from it. It is NOT a dependency: nothing here imports it, nothing imports from it at
# runtime, and the one catalogue file this app validates against is this repository's own
# (frontend/src/components/A2UI/catalogs/), written here.
#
# Kept on disk, kept out of the history. Four copies of the same trees — the clone and
# three folders lifted out of it — would be 105 MB of someone else's code in every clone
# of this repository forever, against the rule above about weight at the root.
/trueforge/
/packages/
/docs/
/python/
/RELEASING.md
/SECURITY.md

# ── VENDORED TREES AND RUNTIME DATA (2026-09-29) ─────────────────────────────
# Four more trees arrived on disk while the ingestion pipeline was read against a real
# implementation. None of them is this repository's source, and measured together they are
# 4,870 MB — against the rule above about weight at the root:
#
#   n8n/                  4,210 MB — the n8n repository, a clone carrying its own .git
#   resources/              334 MB — n8n-master.zip and two more archives under it
#   lit_design-catalogs/    250 MB — third-party design-system archives, read for reference
#   n8n-data/                74 MB — n8n's own runtime directory
#
# Same rule as the vendored reference above: kept on disk for READING, kept out of the
# history. Nothing here is imported, built or served. n8n-data is the one that would be
# worse than heavy — an automation tool's own database holds its credential rows, so
# committing it would put secrets into every clone of this repository forever.
n8n/
resources/
lit_design-catalogs/
n8n-data/

# A dump of THIS repository's database, taken before it is changed. Same rule as the
# .prod-backup-*.json below: insurance, kept on disk, and it holds other people's rows —
# emails, prompt text, password hashes. Never in the history. Written by pg_dump into
# backend/backups/ (custom format, restorable with pg_restore).
/backend/backups/

# A dump of a live database taken before it is changed. It is insurance, it is kept on
# disk, and it holds other people's rows — emails, prompt text, password hashes. Never
# in the history.
.prod-backup-*.json

# A preview is a TEMPORARY FILE, written per ingest and deleted when the designer leaves,
# discards, or asks for something else. It is not source, not a component, and must never be
# committed (backend/routes/figma.py _write_preview_files / _drop_preview_files).
frontend/.preview/

# ── THE VENDORED SHELF AND THE DEVELOPMENT CLONES (2026-10-04) ─────────────────────────────
# Reference material adopted whole, never ours to version: the sample repos under
# wireframe-lab/ and every clone under development/. The ENGINE that the Product room runs on
# IS versioned — inside wireframe-lab/ai-app-builder-open's own git repo (it is that copy's
# local-vcaas/), because it lives beside the app it serves.
wireframe-lab/agent-native/
wireframe-lab/ai-app-builder-open/
wireframe-lab/ai-elements-main/
wireframe-lab/builder-main/
wireframe-lab/chatbot-main/
wireframe-lab/mitosis-main/
development/
